// The element rules of the OFX specification.
//
// The table holds one row for each aggregate of the model of the Python
// library ofxtools: 386 rows, sorted by name, and the 46 enum sets that
// the rows name. A row lists the elements of the aggregate in the order of
// the specification. Each element is TAG:KIND:REQUIRED[:ARGUMENT]. A star
// after the tag marks an element that may repeat. The kinds are:
//   S string, the argument is the length, 0 for no limit
//   I integer, D decimal, T date and time, B flag Y or N
//   E enum, the argument is the index of the set
//   C currency code, K country code, G language code
//   A one aggregate and L a list of aggregates, the argument is the row
//   U a part that ofxtools does not support; it is not checked
// Edit the model and generate the table again, never by hand.
